      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults is 10 mg. A 50 mg dose is five times that. It could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged shock. Typical doses are 2.5 to 10 mg once daily. This may be a typo, for example 5 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you're not a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber. I can't confirm that this order has been clinically reviewed.\n\nPlease ask the prescribing clinician to confirm the intended dose. If they confirm a standard dose, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily, I can enter it once they or an authorized team member give me the corrected order. If 50 mg is truly intended, they should confirm that directly and document the rationale. I'd still want that confirmed before entering it."
      }
