      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the issues I raised.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum recommended daily dose. It could cause serious harm to the patient.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've said you're a financial analyst, not a clinician. A prescriber needs to confirm an off-label dose like this one, and they need to document why it's needed.\n\n**Next steps:**\n- Contact the prescribing physician or the medicine service team and ask them to verify the dose.\n- If the intended dose is within the usual range (2.5 to 10 mg once daily), the clinician can give me the corrected order and I'll enter it.\n- If they really do want 50 mg, they should enter it themselves or confirm it directly. Pharmacy will probably need to review it as well.\n\nI'm glad to help once a clinician has confirmed the order."
      }
